ESMF driver implementation test

This folder contains an ESMF test case. The case aims to test the
implementation of ESMF driver. In this test, a prototype ESMF driver will run,
but the driver is not driving "real" ocean/atmosphere models.


The scripts resolve their own locations, so they can be launched from any
working directory. To build from a clean solver directory and run with five
MPI ranks::

  export ESMFMKFILE=/path/to/esmf.mk
  ./install.sh -j8

Build and run can also be invoked separately::

  ./coupledSolver/Allmake.sh -j8
  MPI_RANKS=5 ./run/Allrun

`MPIEXEC` selects the launcher (default `mpirun`) and `MPIEXEC_NP_FLAG` selects
its process-count option (default `-np`). `MPI_RANKS` must be a positive
integer. A missing executable, configuration, launcher, or invalid rank count
causes an immediate non-zero exit.

To clean this case::

  ./clean.sh --dry-run
  ./clean.sh

`Allclean` only removes the staged executable, staged configuration, ESMF log
files, and diagnostic NetCDF names produced by this L1.C2 case. It never uses
recursive deletion or broad `*.*`, `wrf*`, `ncep*`, or `log*` patterns.
`clean.sh` also removes recognized solver build products and does not require
`ESMFMKFILE`.

Folders:

  ./coupledSolver: Source code for the ESMF test case
  ./run: The simulation will run in this folder.

####################
WARNING!!!WARNING!!!
####################
ESMF must be installed to run this case. Before building, set `ESMFMKFILE` to
the `esmf.mk` file from the ESMF installation. The variable may also be passed
directly to make. For example::

  export ESMFMKFILE=/path/to/esmf.mk
  cd coupledSolver
  make -j

The runtime configuration file `coupledSolver/namelist.rc` is required and
must contain a non-negative integer `DebugLevel:` setting. `DebugLevel: 0` is
the portable control-flow test used by default. Values greater than or equal
to 1 enable diagnostic array output and require an ESMF build with PIO support;
the application reports this requirement during startup if PIO is unavailable.
